[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When flying your drone, you can use guards to protect your propellers and ensure flights are safe and [music] smooth. The letters under the propeller guard clips represent the following orientations. [music] L front left, FR front right,'

[00:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'BL rear left, [music] BR rear right. Before installation, open all four clips on the propeller guard. [music] Connect'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the front left L and rear left BR sections of the frame. Then connect the front right F FR and rear right BR sections. [music] Unfold the drone arms with the tail'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'facing toward you. [music] First, insert the front arm feet into'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the designated slots. Push the front arms [music] downward into the slots. Then adjust the rear arms and snap them into their corresponding slots. Spread'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the propellers apart. Close the clips and press firmly until you hear a click indicating the clips are locked. Install the left side propeller guard in'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the same way. [music] &gt;&gt; [music]'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; After installation, take off and hover. Once the vision goggles display [music] the message, propeller guards detected,'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you may begin flying. [music] Thanks for watching.'
